Upstream: https://github.com/confluentinc/librdkafka/pull/5636 (head e8b63ae1e3d4)
Fixes:    https://github.com/confluentinc/librdkafka/issues/5632
Subject:  Idempotent producer: cap in-flight ProduceRequests, not messages

The idempotent per-partition in-flight limit subtracted rktp_msgs_inflight (a
MESSAGE count) from RD_KAFKA_IDEMP_MAX_INFLIGHT (a REQUEST limit), so a
partition with five records in flight could not start another request. The
broker's de-duplication window is five batches, and kafka-clients allows five
requests per partition. Source hunks of the upstream PR only (CHANGELOG and the
mock test omitted), rebased onto librdkafka 2.12.1 as bundled by
rdkafka-sys 4.10.0+2.12.1.

diff -ru -x *.orig a/librdkafka/src/rdkafka_broker.c b/librdkafka/src/rdkafka_broker.c
--- a/librdkafka/src/rdkafka_broker.c	2026-11-16 19:55:49
+++ b/librdkafka/src/rdkafka_broker.c	2026-11-16 19:55:50
@@ -4030,7 +4030,7 @@
                                     rkb, QUEUE, "TOPPAR",
                                     "%.*s [%" PRId32
                                     "] waiting for "
-                                    "%d in-flight request(s) to drain "
+                                    "%d in-flight message(s) to drain "
                                     "from queue before continuing "
                                     "to produce",
                                     RD_KAFKAP_STR_PR(rktp->rktp_rkt->rkt_topic),
@@ -4060,8 +4060,10 @@
 
                 /* Limit the number of in-flight requests (per partition)
                  * to the broker's sequence de-duplication window. */
-                max_requests = RD_MIN(max_requests,
-                                      RD_KAFKA_IDEMP_MAX_INFLIGHT - inflight);
+                max_requests =
+                    RD_MIN(max_requests,
+                           RD_KAFKA_IDEMP_MAX_INFLIGHT -
+                               rd_atomic32_get(&rktp->rktp_reqs_inflight));
         }
 
 
